ORIGIN OF THE CONTENT
---------------------
Every workflow, script, prompt and document in this repository was written for
this repository or rewritten for it. No file is a copy of a third-party
template, gallery entry or tutorial.

Several templates implement patterns that are widely documented in public
material: the enrich-verify-suppress sequence used in outbound email, the
config-at-the-head-of-the-graph convention in visual workflow tools, the
invocable-method bridge between Salesforce Apex and Flow, the sensor-and-asset
model in data orchestrators, and the structured-output-with-repair loop in LLM
pipelines. Patterns are not copyrightable; the expression here is original. Where
a template follows published guidance, its README cites the source under a
"Prior art" heading so a reader can check the original.

FIXTURE AND SAMPLE DATA
-----------------------
All organisations, people, addresses, phone numbers and domains in sample data
are invented. Every fixture domain sits under the .example top-level domain,
which RFC 2606 reserves and which therefore cannot resolve or receive mail.
Phone numbers use the 555-01xx range reserved for fictional use. Any resemblance
to a real organisation is coincidental and unintended; open an issue and it will
be changed.

